      "title": "A baffling trail from Australia to Singapore: what is Megaspeed, the company implicated in downfall of Nvidia’s Jensen Huang?",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/13/a-baffling-trail-from-australia-to-singapore-what-is-megaspeed-the-company-implicated-in-downfall-of-nvidias-jensen-huang",
      "description": "<p>Few solid clues have emerged as to the true nature of Megaspeed, whose former director Alice Huang has been accused of being a Chinese spy</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/12/rise-and-fall-of-nvidia-ceo-jensen-huang-profile\">From washing dishes at Denny’s to rockstar of AI: the rise and fall of Jensen Huang</a></p></li></ul><p>A lottery retailer in rural Australia, a dilapidated storefront in Kuala Lumpur, and a near-empty office in Singapore: the global facades of Megaspeed International, the company linked to the downfall of Nvidia chief Jensen Huang, form a puzzling corporate picture.</p><p>The company, which is registered in Singapore, has registered affiliates across the US, Asia and Australia, but individuals at its offices say they know nothing about the cloud computing firm at the centre of a global spy scandal.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/nov/13/a-baffling-trail-from-australia-to-singapore-what-is-megaspeed-the-company-implicated-in-downfall-of-nvidias-jensen-huang\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-13T07:07:41"
    },
    {
      "title": "Victoria election 2026: Labor and Greens trade accusations of ‘dodgy deals’ as preference fight puts key seats at risk",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/13/victoria-state-election-2026-labor-greens-preference-deals-seats",
      "description": "<p>Greens say they will not direct preferences to Labor in 15 seats after party’s ‘unforgivable’ decision earlier in week</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Greens have retaliated against Labor’s decision to run an open ticket in a key inner-city seat by refusing to direct preferences to the party in 15 electorates across the state at this month’s Victorian election.</p><p>The move has sparked a war of words between the two parties, with each accusing the other of striking a “dodgy deal” that could help the Liberals and One Nation get elected on 28 November.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/13/victoria-state-election-2026-labor-greens-preference-deals-seats\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-13T06:16:06"
    },
